  "question": {
    "text": "<math><mi>P</mi></math> - <math><mi>V</mi></math> diagram of an ideal gas is shown. The gas undergoes from initial state <math> <mi>A</mi> </math> to final state <math> <mi>B</mi> </math> such that initial and final volumes are same. Select the correct alternative for given process <math> <mrow> <mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow> </math>.<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0111_e3aab4e84b78.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 161px; height: 131px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Work done by gas is positive",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Work done by gas is negative",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Temperature of gas increases continuously",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Process is isochoric",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0111_df9d170ef22e.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 142px; height: 125px;\" /><br /><br />Volume does not remain constant throughout the process <math> <mrow>  <mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></math>. As <math><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>, temperature decreases initially as both <math> <mi>P</mi></math> and <math> <mi>V</mi></math> decreases. By area under curve, net work done is negative."
  }
}